===Etymology===
From {{etyl|roa-opt|pt}} {{m|roa-opt|temer}}, {{etyl|la|pt}} {{m|la|timēre}}, present active infinitive of {{m|la|timeō||I fear}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Paulista}} {{IPA|/te.ˈme(ɹ)/|lang=pt}}
* {{a|South Brazil}} {{IPA|/te.ˈme(ɻ)/|lang=pt}}
* {{a|PT}} {{IPA|/tɨ.ˈmeɾ/|lang=pt}}
* {{hyphenation|te|mer|lang=pt}}

===Verb===
{{pt-verb|tem|er}}

# to [[fear]] {{gloss|to feel fear about something}}
# {{label|pt|chiefly|theology}} to [[fear]] {{gloss|to venerate; to feel awe towards}}
# to be [[afraid]] {{gloss|regretful, sorry}}
#: {{ux|pt|'''Temo''' que não posso ajudar.|'''I’m afraid''' I can’t help.|inline=1}}

